{"check": {"imports": [], "kind": "asserts", "reference": "def rgb_to_hsv(r, g, b):\n    r, g, b = r/255.0, g/255.0, b/255.0\n    mx = max(r, g, b)\n    mn = min(r, g, b)\n    df = mx-mn\n    if mx == mn:\n        h = 0\n    elif mx == r:\n        h = (60 * ((g-b)/df) + 360) % 360\n    elif mx == g:\n        h = (60 * ((b-r)/df) + 120) % 360\n    elif mx == b:\n        h = (60 * ((r-g)/df) + 240) % 360\n    if mx == 0:\n        s = 0\n    else:\n        s = (df/mx)*100\n    v = mx*100\n    return h, s, v", "tests": ["assert rgb_to_hsv(255, 255, 255)==(0, 0.0, 100.0)", "assert rgb_to_hsv(0, 215, 0)==(120.0, 100.0, 84.31372549019608)", "assert rgb_to_hsv(10, 215, 110)==(149.26829268292684, 95.34883720930233, 84.31372549019608)"]}, "id": "w9-mbpp-783", "prompt": "Write the Python function described below. You may run code to check it. End with the complete Python code in a fenced block.\n\nWrite a function to convert rgb color to hsv color. https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/program-change-rgb-color-model-hsv-color-model/\nYour code should pass this test:\nassert rgb_to_hsv(255, 255, 255)==(0, 0.0, 100.0)", "semantic_sha256": "bc37486927f161f6b3ba59e475bcf2779d256c927607f916858c93fffd4a8181", "set": "mbpp", "source_lineage": "sanitized-mbpp/task_id/783", "source_prompt": "Write a function to convert rgb color to hsv color. https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/program-change-rgb-color-model-hsv-color-model/"}
